  "0_outline_root": "ROOT: Contract Commitment Duration Type > Requirements",
  "0_outline_lines": [
    "L016: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType MUST adhere to the following requirements:\"",
    "  L018: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType MUST be of type String.\"",
    "  L019: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType MUST conform to [StringHandling](#attributes.stringhandling) requirements.\"",
    "  L020: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType MUST NOT be null.\"",
    "  L021: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType SHOULD be expressed with a quantity and time unit, where quantity is a positive integer, and time-unit is a standardized unit of time, either singular or plural (e.g., \\\"1 Day\\\", \\\"1 Year\\\", \\\"3 Months\\\", \\\"3 Years\\\").\"",
    "  L022: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType SHOULD present the unit of time as one of the allowed values.\"",
    "  L023: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType SHOULD correspond to the standard duration of the purchased offering (e.g., \\\"1 Year\\\", \\\"3 Years\\\") rather than a precise calculation of days or hours.\"",
    "  L024: \"ContractCommitmentDurationType MAY differ from the actual duration calculated between [ContractCommitmentPeriodStart](#datasets.contractcommitment.contractcommitmentperiodstart) and [ContractCommitmentPeriodEnd](#datasets.contractcommitment.contractcommitmentperiodend) (e.g., if a 3-year commitment is exchanged in its final month, the resulting record may have a short lifespan but retains a value of \\\"3 Years\\\").\""
  ],
